{% comment %}
  Renders product variant-picker

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} product object.
  - block: {Object} passing the block information.
  - product_form_id: {String} Id of the product form to which the variant picker is associated.
  Usage:
  {% render 'product-variant-picker', product: product, block: block, product_form_id: product_form_id %}
{% endcomment %}
{%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
  {% comment %}
    Cullinan: a colour option that only mirrors a material option is not drawn.

    The option with swatches exists so the product cards can show colour circles. On
    the product page the shopper chooses the material, in words, and the colour follows
    from it -- drawn as well, the two rows would say the same thing twice.

    An option with swatches is skipped only when another option, without swatches,
    covers it exactly: every value of that option contains exactly one colour name, and
    every colour name sits inside at least one value ("жълто злато" inside "14К жълто
    злато"). Anything short of that draws both rows as Dawn does, so a choice can never
    become unreachable, and a product with a colour option alone keeps its picker.

    The skipped option is still part of every variant, so it cannot just be left out of
    the request: Shopify would fill it with its first value and a shopper choosing rose
    gold could be sent a variant whose colour says yellow. product-variant-options.liquid
    sends the matching colour's id together with each visible value instead (`twin`).
  {% endcomment %}
  {%- liquid
    assign hidden_option = null
    assign shown_option = null

    for candidate in product.options_with_values
      assign candidate_swatches = candidate.values | map: 'swatch' | compact | size
      if candidate_swatches > 0
        assign hidden_option = candidate
        break
      endif
    endfor

    if hidden_option
      for candidate in product.options_with_values
        if shown_option
          break
        endif
        assign candidate_swatches = candidate.values | map: 'swatch' | compact | size
        if candidate.position == hidden_option.position or candidate_swatches > 0
          continue
        endif

        assign pairing_ok = true
        for candidate_value in candidate.values
          assign candidate_name = candidate_value.name | downcase
          assign name_matches = 0
          for hidden_value in hidden_option.values
            assign hidden_name = hidden_value.name | downcase
            if hidden_name != blank and candidate_name contains hidden_name
              assign name_matches = name_matches | plus: 1
            endif
          endfor
          if name_matches != 1
            assign pairing_ok = false
          endif
        endfor

        for hidden_value in hidden_option.values
          assign hidden_name = hidden_value.name | downcase
          assign name_found = false
          for candidate_value in candidate.values
            assign candidate_name = candidate_value.name | downcase
            if hidden_name != blank and candidate_name contains hidden_name
              assign name_found = true
            endif
          endfor
          unless name_found
            assign pairing_ok = false
          endunless
        endfor

        if pairing_ok
          assign shown_option = candidate
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  -%}
  <variant-selects
    id="variant-selects-{{ section.id }}"
    data-section="{{ section.id }}"
    data-product-handle="{{ product.handle }}"
    data-product-title="{{ product.title | escape }}"
    data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
    data-currency-code="{{ cart.currency.iso_code }}"
    {% # theme-check-disable %}
    data-selected-price-amount="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price | default: 0 | money_amount | escape }}"
    {% # theme-check-enable %}
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    {%- comment -%}
      Cullinan: the metal or material is chosen first, the size after it
      (2026-10-01, the owner: the ring size and "choosing your materials" swap).
      Shopify draws options in the order the product lists them -- size, colour,
      metal on the ring -- and that order lives in the Admin, so the theme draws
      the options twice, once for the ones whose name says metal or material and
      once for the rest, each pass in the product's own order. Nothing but the
      order on the page changes: the radios still carry their own ids, which is
      all the request to Shopify is built from, and the cart, checkout and emails
      list the options in the Admin's order as before. A product with no such
      option draws exactly as it did.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- for pass in (1..2) -%}
    {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
      {%- if shown_option and option.position == hidden_option.position -%}
        {%- continue -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign option_name_lower = option.name | downcase
        assign is_material = false
        if option_name_lower contains 'метал' or option_name_lower contains 'материал' or option_name_lower contains 'metal' or option_name_lower contains 'material'
          assign is_material = true
        endif
      -%}
      {%- if pass == 1 and is_material == false -%}
        {%- continue -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if pass == 2 and is_material -%}
        {%- continue -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign swatch_count = option.values | map: 'swatch' | compact | size
        assign picker_type = block.settings.picker_type

        assign twin = null
        if shown_option and option.position == shown_option.position
          assign twin = hidden_option
        endif

        if swatch_count > 0 and block.settings.swatch_shape != 'none'
          if block.settings.picker_type == 'dropdown'
            assign picker_type = 'swatch_dropdown'
          else
            assign picker_type = 'swatch'
          endif
        endif

        assign use_menu = false
        if is_material and picker_type == 'button' and option.values.size > 1
          assign use_menu = true
        endif
      -%}
      {%- if picker_type == 'swatch' -%}
        <fieldset class="js product-form__input product-form__input--swatch">
          <legend class="form__label">
            {{ option.name }}:
            <span data-selected-value>
              {{- option.selected_value -}}
            </span>
          </legend>
          {% render 'product-variant-options',
            product: product,
            option: option,
            block: block,
            picker_type: picker_type,
            twin: twin
          %}
        </fieldset>
      {%- elsif use_menu -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Cullinan: the metal or material as a drop-down menu instead of a row of
          buttons of four different widths (2026-10-01, the owner, after
          moonmagic's "Choose your metal": "i want the buttons to be the same size,
          or you can make them not buttons but something else ... with drop down
          menu"). The legend keeps the option's own name; the box under it shows the
          current choice, the way moonmagic's row does, and opens the list.

          The list is the option's own radio inputs, so <variant-selects> reads and
          sends them exactly as it does the pills (`fieldset input:checked`) and
          Dawn's `[data-selected-value]` update lands in the box. <option-menu>
          (assets/option-menu.js) only adds what a menu needs on top: closing on a
          pick, on Escape and on a click outside, and keeping keyboard focus in
          place across Dawn's re-render of the whole picker. Without the script it
          is still a working <details>.

          The dot is the colour this value stands for: its own swatch, or the hidden
          colour option's swatch when this option stands in for it (`twin`).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign menu_dot = null
          assign menu_dot_source = option.selected_value
          if twin
            assign selected_down = option.selected_value.name | downcase
            for twin_candidate in twin.values
              assign twin_down = twin_candidate.name | downcase
              if twin_down != blank and selected_down contains twin_down
                assign menu_dot_source = twin_candidate
              endif
            endfor
          endif
          if menu_dot_source.swatch.image
            assign menu_dot = menu_dot_source.swatch.image | image_url: width: 50 | prepend: 'url(' | append: ')'
          elsif menu_dot_source.swatch.color
            assign menu_dot = 'rgb(' | append: menu_dot_source.swatch.color.rgb | append: ')'
          endif
        -%}
        <fieldset class="js product-form__input product-form__input--menu">
          <legend class="form__label">{{ option.name }}</legend>
          <option-menu data-key="{{ section.id }}-{{ option.position }}">
            <details class="option-menu">
              <summary class="option-menu__summary">
                <span
                  class="option-menu__dot"
                  {% if menu_dot %}
                    style="--option-dot: {{ menu_dot }};"
                  {% else %}
                    hidden
                  {% endif %}
                ></span>
                <span class="option-menu__current" data-selected-value>
                  {{- option.selected_value -}}
                </span>
                {{- 'icon-caret.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
              </summary>
              <div class="option-menu__list">
                {% render 'product-variant-options',
                  product: product,
                  option: option,
                  block: block,
                  picker_type: 'menu',
                  twin: twin
                %}
              </div>
            </details>
          </option-menu>
        </fieldset>
      {%- elsif picker_type == 'button' -%}
        <fieldset class="js product-form__input product-form__input--pill">
          <legend class="form__label">
            {{ option.name }}:
            <span data-selected-value>
              {{- option.selected_value -}}
            </span>
          </legend>
          {% render 'product-variant-options',
            product: product,
            option: option,
            block: block,
            picker_type: picker_type,
            twin: twin
          %}
        </fieldset>
      {%- else -%}
        <div class="product-form__input product-form__input--dropdown">
          <label class="form__label" for="Option-{{ section.id }}-{{ option.position }}">
            {{ option.name }}
          </label>
          <div class="select">
            {%- if picker_type == 'swatch_dropdown' -%}
              <span
                data-selected-value
                class="dropdown-swatch"
              >
                {% render 'swatch', swatch: option.selected_value.swatch, shape: block.settings.swatch_shape %}
              </span>
            {%- endif -%}
            <select
              id="Option-{{ section.id }}-{{ option.position }}"
              class="select__select"
              name="options[{{ option.name | escape }}]"
              form="{{ product_form_id }}"
            >
              {% render 'product-variant-options',
                product: product,
                option: option,
                block: block,
                picker_type: picker_type,
                twin: twin
              %}
            </select>
            <span class="svg-wrapper">
              {{- 'icon-caret.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endfor -%}

    <script type="application/json" data-selected-variant>
      {{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant | json }}
    </script>
  </variant-selects>
{%- endunless -%}
